-- Mob AI: ClassAiRules seed (WP-B of ops/plans/mob-ai.md).
--
-- Hand-ported from the legacy hard-coded mob AI lists (cleric.cpp, sorcerer.cpp, rogue.cpp,
-- warrior.cpp, mobact.cpp) into per-class rule lists. Generated by
-- `python -m fierylib.seeders.mob_ai_seeder --write-sql` from data/mob_ai_seed.json; a unit
-- test keeps the two in sync. Requires 2026-10-10-mob-ai-schema.sql.
--
-- A rule is created only for a class that really has the ability (ClassAbilities for spells,
-- songs and chants, ClassSkills for skills; the skill's min_level becomes min_level). Keyed by
-- Class.plain_name / Ability.plain_name, never numeric ids.
--
-- Ownership: every seed rule has a stable seed_key (<Class>/<family>:<ABILITY>) and a seed_hash of
-- the values it last wrote (chance, cooldown, conditions, target, min_level, priority, ability;
-- `enabled` is not part of it). The three statements (a) claim existing un-keyed rows that still
-- match the seed, (b) upsert on seed_key, updating a row only while its stored hash equals the
-- hash of its current values, so a row a builder edited (Muditor clears seed_hash) is left alone and
-- renumbering a priority updates the row instead of duplicating it, and (c) disable seed-owned
-- rows whose key left the seed. Builder-created rows have no seed_key. A second run changes 0 rows.
-- Race rules (dragon breath, sweep, roar) are in 2026-10-10-mob-ai-race.sql.

BEGIN;

ALTER TABLE "ClassAiRules"
    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "seed_key" TEXT,
    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "seed_hash" TEXT;

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS "ClassAiRules_seed_key_key" ON "ClassAiRules"("seed_key");

